WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.834 --> 00:00:03.036
 Alex, Kevin, congratulations.

00:00:03.102 --> 00:00:04.537
You guys are in the
third and final round

00:00:04.603 --> 00:00:06.673
of this competition, which
means that you're both one

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:09.108
step closer to the title
of Forged in Fire Champion

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:10.943
and a check for $10,000.

00:00:10.977 --> 00:00:12.444
All you need to
do now is go home

00:00:12.478 --> 00:00:15.682
and recreate this iconic
weapon from history--

00:00:19.686 --> 00:00:21.821
the spatha.

00:00:21.888 --> 00:00:22.922
Good luck, bladesmiths.

00:00:22.989 --> 00:00:24.556
We'll see you in four days.

00:00:24.623 --> 00:00:25.324
 Good luck.

00:00:25.391 --> 00:00:26.159
 Kevin.

00:00:31.197 --> 00:00:33.700
 So it's day one in
Belleville, West Virginia.

00:00:33.766 --> 00:00:34.967
I've got a spatha to go make.

00:00:35.001 --> 00:00:35.935
Let's get crack-a-lacking.

00:00:36.002 --> 00:00:38.004
Woo!

00:00:38.071 --> 00:00:40.106
I'm gonna be using 51-60.

00:00:40.139 --> 00:00:41.473
It's a forgiving medium.

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:43.242
It'll bring some strength
to whatever they're

00:00:43.275 --> 00:00:45.978
gonna smash, cut, break, kill.

00:00:46.011 --> 00:00:49.315
So I'm gonna try Big
Sexy first to bash down

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:51.284
the width of that
material to about two

00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:53.520
and a half, two and a
quarter inches wide.

00:00:57.590 --> 00:00:58.490
Come on, dang it.

00:00:58.557 --> 00:00:59.259
Work.

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:04.163
Four days isn't enough
time to make a spatha.

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:07.199
You don't know what the
complications are gonna be.

00:01:07.266 --> 00:01:09.302
She's getting there, though.

00:01:09.368 --> 00:01:11.003
I slowly started drawing it out.

00:01:11.037 --> 00:01:12.605
I'm about 35 inches long.

00:01:12.672 --> 00:01:14.340
You know, it's just
patience, getting

00:01:14.407 --> 00:01:15.641
the equipment to work right.

00:01:15.708 --> 00:01:18.277
Tomorrow, pressure
will be on, because I

00:01:18.343 --> 00:01:20.012
gotta get this thing quenched.

00:01:20.045 --> 00:01:21.948
If I don't, I'm behind the ball.

00:01:22.015 --> 00:01:22.749
Woo!

00:01:26.552 --> 00:01:29.889 line:0%
 Definitely excited to be
back home, back in my shop,

00:01:29.922 --> 00:01:31.457 line:7%
where I'm nice and comfortable.

00:01:31.524 --> 00:01:34.994
I'm gonna do a full Damascus
blade with a little bit

00:01:35.061 --> 00:01:37.162
of a ladder pattern in it.

00:01:37.229 --> 00:01:39.165
I'm really looking
forward to going all out

00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:42.668
and making something really
cool to impress the judges.

00:01:42.701 --> 00:01:45.905
First press was just nice
and quick and light, just

00:01:45.938 --> 00:01:47.573
to push everything together.

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:50.276
This next press will be
a little more aggressive.

00:01:50.343 --> 00:01:54.113
Probably the most important
part of this entire weld.

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:56.015
My weld seemed to have
stuck pretty well.

00:01:56.048 --> 00:01:57.584
I'm gonna start
drawing this thing out.

00:02:02.488 --> 00:02:04.590
I've got one seam
that came apart.

00:02:04.623 --> 00:02:07.960
I think if I just flux it, get
it hot, and press it again,

00:02:08.027 --> 00:02:09.128
should be OK.

00:02:09.195 --> 00:02:11.064
Let's hope.

00:02:11.131 --> 00:02:14.467
This might be a make-or-break
moment right here.

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:16.235
I really hope
that's the only one,

00:02:16.302 --> 00:02:18.704
but deep down, I'm
petrified that there

00:02:18.771 --> 00:02:20.873
is gonna be more of
these seams opening

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:21.808
up throughout this billet.

00:02:24.377 --> 00:02:25.912
As I go to start
drawing this billet out,

00:02:25.978 --> 00:02:29.481
a big seam just opens up right
in the center of my billet.

00:02:29.515 --> 00:02:31.651
So I think my best
bet is gonna be

00:02:31.717 --> 00:02:35.955
to break this billet in half,
salvage as much welded steel

00:02:35.988 --> 00:02:37.756
as I possibly can.

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:42.194
And I'll just do a generic
random pattern Damascus.

00:02:42.227 --> 00:02:46.232
But it'll still be
a Damascus sword.

00:02:46.299 --> 00:02:48.567
Well, the good news is both
of those seem really solid.

00:02:48.634 --> 00:02:52.438 line:0%
So at least we got
something out of that.

00:02:52.505 --> 00:02:54.073 line:0%
KEVIN (VOICEOVER):
Today, I need to get

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:56.242 line:7%
the blade done and quenched.

00:02:56.308 --> 00:02:58.377
So I got the shoulders put in.

00:02:58.410 --> 00:03:01.214
I have the medial ridge, where
you can distinctly see where

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:03.282
it's starting to come together.

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:04.584
It's time for the quench.

00:03:08.488 --> 00:03:09.455
Ah, [bleep].

00:03:12.825 --> 00:03:15.195
Look at that [bleep] end.

00:03:15.261 --> 00:03:18.531
We're quenching again, because
I don't have time to eff

00:03:18.564 --> 00:03:19.966
around with the normalization.

00:03:20.032 --> 00:03:22.901
Because I went all the way down
to the bottom, and I felt it

00:03:22.968 --> 00:03:24.137
bend.

00:03:24.204 --> 00:03:26.806
I got to go through all
the steps all over again.

00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:33.212
Still got that bend.

00:03:33.279 --> 00:03:34.680
I'm gonna temper overnight.

00:03:34.747 --> 00:03:39.619
And in that process, it'll start
to, hopefully, normalize down.

00:03:39.652 --> 00:03:40.686
It's hit or miss.

00:03:40.753 --> 00:03:43.289
It's either gonna go well,
or it's gonna go wrong.

00:03:43.322 --> 00:03:45.625
And, yeah, it went wrong today.

00:03:47.726 --> 00:03:49.261 line:0%
ALEX (VOICEOVER): It's
the morning of day two.

00:03:49.328 --> 00:03:51.397
Definitely got some
setbacks yesterday.

00:03:51.463 --> 00:03:53.432
Starting the day with
my billet tacked up

00:03:53.465 --> 00:03:54.900
and ready for forge welding.

00:03:54.967 --> 00:03:59.705
And hoping to end the day with
a quenched and hardened spatha.

00:03:59.772 --> 00:04:00.506
First press.

00:04:04.076 --> 00:04:05.211
Looks OK so far.

00:04:05.278 --> 00:04:08.381 line:0%
But I'm still gonna
be really careful.

00:04:08.448 --> 00:04:11.818 line:0%
I've got my billet drawn
out pretty close to shape.

00:04:11.884 --> 00:04:13.652
I have just enough length there.

00:04:13.719 --> 00:04:18.124
You can see, I'm kind of forging
in that medial ridge already.

00:04:18.157 --> 00:04:21.995
This is the longest blade I
have ever attempted to quench.

00:04:24.596 --> 00:04:27.099
I pull the blade out of the
oil at the end of the day.

00:04:27.165 --> 00:04:29.002
I have an intact Damascus blade.

00:04:29.068 --> 00:04:30.269
First thing tomorrow,
I'm gonna get

00:04:30.336 --> 00:04:32.304
my blade etched and
the handle prepared

00:04:32.371 --> 00:04:34.274
and looking forward
to a good day.

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:38.444 line:0%
 I'm feeling better
than last night,

00:04:38.477 --> 00:04:42.214 line:0%
because I got the blade
tempered and got it straight.

00:04:42.281 --> 00:04:43.716
Still behind the ball.

00:04:43.749 --> 00:04:45.751
I'm gonna start to
fit up the handle,

00:04:45.784 --> 00:04:49.555
start looking at different parts
to what I think looks well.

00:04:49.622 --> 00:04:51.557
So my design plan
for this pommel

00:04:51.624 --> 00:04:53.626
is I'm gonna take two
ends of the deer antler,

00:04:53.693 --> 00:04:57.229
and I'm going to carve a
lion's head out of them.

00:04:57.296 --> 00:05:00.132
Hand-carving anything
is time-consuming,

00:05:00.198 --> 00:05:02.334
so I can't get lost in my head.

00:05:02.368 --> 00:05:04.736
I'll set it in on top of
glow in the dark resin.

00:05:04.770 --> 00:05:06.839
And then I'll fill that
in with a clear epoxy.

00:05:06.906 --> 00:05:09.542
I'm not walking in there
with something plain.

00:05:09.608 --> 00:05:11.711
Tomorrow, I'm gonna
put some bronze medal

00:05:11.778 --> 00:05:12.744
stain on the blade.

00:05:12.811 --> 00:05:14.880
And I'm gonna finish
this no matter what.

00:05:14.947 --> 00:05:17.383 line:7%
It'll be done.

00:05:17.449 --> 00:05:18.517 line:0%
ALEX (VOICEOVER):
Start of day four.

00:05:18.584 --> 00:05:20.119 line:0%
Fatigue of the
past couple days is

00:05:20.152 --> 00:05:21.387 line:7%
definitely starting to set in.

00:05:21.454 --> 00:05:23.389
The blade's been etched
in the coffee overnight

00:05:23.423 --> 00:05:25.391
to really bring
out the contrast.

00:05:25.457 --> 00:05:28.895
Yeah, it really
darkened up that 10-84.

00:05:28.961 --> 00:05:31.597
So the spatha needs
to have a wooden guard

00:05:31.664 --> 00:05:33.099
and a disk shaped pommel.

00:05:33.132 --> 00:05:35.468
So I'm going to do
a stacked handle.

00:05:35.535 --> 00:05:38.204
I'm using iron wood for
the guard and the pommel,

00:05:38.271 --> 00:05:39.571
because it's super strong.

00:05:39.638 --> 00:05:41.974
And then I'm gonna use
blackwood for the main part

00:05:42.041 --> 00:05:43.276
of the handle.

00:05:43.343 --> 00:05:46.212
I've got all my individual
pieces of this handle.

00:05:46.279 --> 00:05:48.547
Fit it up nice and tight.

00:05:48.580 --> 00:05:49.781
Got to get this blade sharpened.

00:05:49.848 --> 00:05:51.517
I've never sharpened
anything this long before,

00:05:51.583 --> 00:05:53.819
but I know how to put
an edge on a knife.

00:05:53.853 --> 00:05:55.955
I cannot wait to see this
thing put to the test.

00:06:02.094 --> 00:06:03.229
Word.

00:06:03.295 --> 00:06:05.498
 All right, bladesmiths, your
spatha swords look amazing.

00:06:05.564 --> 00:06:08.367
But it's time to find out
what kind of lethal damage

00:06:08.433 --> 00:06:09.469
that they can do.

00:06:09.535 --> 00:06:10.869
To do that, I will
take your weapon,

00:06:10.936 --> 00:06:14.173
deliver some killing slashes
and blows on this more

00:06:14.239 --> 00:06:16.341
than willing ballistics dummy.

00:06:16.408 --> 00:06:17.176
Alex, you're up first.

00:06:17.243 --> 00:06:18.010
You ready for this?

00:06:18.077 --> 00:06:18.778
 Let's do it.

00:06:22.981 --> 00:06:29.522
[blade impacts]

00:06:51.911 --> 00:06:54.046
All right, Alex,
first up, I can really

00:06:54.113 --> 00:06:57.082
appreciate the beauty that you
have with your Damascus pattern

00:06:57.149 --> 00:06:57.950
right there.

00:06:58.017 --> 00:06:59.552
It really stands out.

00:06:59.618 --> 00:07:01.720
Very clean lines.

00:07:01.787 --> 00:07:03.789
The medial ridge
you have on here,

00:07:03.856 --> 00:07:05.324
I can imagine how
much work that takes

00:07:05.391 --> 00:07:08.961
to get it almost perfectly
straight all the way

00:07:08.995 --> 00:07:10.096
through to the tip.

00:07:10.163 --> 00:07:13.365
Your tip is sharp enough
to penetrate with a thrust

00:07:13.432 --> 00:07:15.168
and lacerate on the way out.

00:07:15.234 --> 00:07:18.103
And most importantly,
it will kill.

00:07:18.170 --> 00:07:18.937
 Thank you.

00:07:19.004 --> 00:07:20.306
 Good job.

00:07:20.373 --> 00:07:21.474
All right, Kevin,
it's your turn.

00:07:21.540 --> 00:07:22.374
So are you ready?

00:07:22.407 --> 00:07:23.142
 Hell yeah.

00:07:23.209 --> 00:07:24.844
 Let's do this.

00:07:24.910 --> 00:07:28.780
 Alex's spatha just destroyed
that ballistics dummy.

00:07:28.814 --> 00:07:31.717
And now, I'm feeling
anxious, excited.

00:07:31.784 --> 00:07:33.119
I got the adrenaline going.

00:07:44.497 --> 00:07:45.797
- There's no medial ridge.
- Let me see.

00:07:45.864 --> 00:07:46.599
 What's up?

00:07:48.567 --> 00:07:50.569
No medial ridge on
either side of the blade?

00:07:50.635 --> 00:07:51.970
 That's one of the parameters.

00:07:52.037 --> 00:07:52.738
 Right?

00:07:57.976 --> 00:08:00.613
 Kevin, your blade must
fall within our parameters

00:08:00.680 --> 00:08:04.950
in order to be tested evenly and
fairly with your competitors.

00:08:04.983 --> 00:08:07.620
Your blade does not
have a central ridge.

00:08:07.687 --> 00:08:09.422
That was a parameter
that was outlined

00:08:09.488 --> 00:08:10.889
before we ever sent you home.

00:08:10.956 --> 00:08:14.894
And for that reason, you cannot
be the Forged in Fire Champion.

00:08:14.961 --> 00:08:16.762
Come on, my friend.

00:08:16.828 --> 00:08:18.931
 You know, it's just a
bummer I can't see it tested.

00:08:18.998 --> 00:08:20.399
That's what I really
wanted to see.

00:08:20.465 --> 00:08:21.566
I want to see how it holds up.

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:23.035
 Nice work on that handle.

00:08:23.068 --> 00:08:23.569
 Thank you.

00:08:23.636 --> 00:08:24.870
I appreciate it.

00:08:24.937 --> 00:08:28.407
When I was making it, it
had the defined ridge in it.

00:08:28.440 --> 00:08:30.443
Just with the
sanding and grinding,

00:08:30.476 --> 00:08:31.910
it just took more of it off.

00:08:31.977 --> 00:08:34.280
But this whole experience
has been a blast.

00:08:34.346 --> 00:08:35.547
 Congratulations.

00:08:35.580 --> 00:08:36.849
KEVIN (VOICEOVER):
This isn't a loss.

00:08:36.882 --> 00:08:41.920
I'm coming home with
a $10,000 experience.

00:08:41.987 --> 00:08:45.324
 Alex, you made a
sharp and deadly spatha,

00:08:45.390 --> 00:08:47.326
but not only that,
you made something

00:08:47.359 --> 00:08:49.228
that is detailed and beautiful.

00:08:49.295 --> 00:08:53.198
Your attention to detail has
elevated you to the title

00:08:53.265 --> 00:08:55.100
of Forged in Fire Champion.

00:08:55.167 --> 00:08:56.135
Congratulations.

00:08:56.168 --> 00:08:59.471
Your title comes with
a check for $10,000.

00:08:59.504 --> 00:09:00.673
Good job, brother.

00:09:00.740 --> 00:09:01.973
ALEX (VOICEOVER):
This is pretty wild.

00:09:02.007 --> 00:09:04.443
I came here to challenge
myself and put myself

00:09:04.509 --> 00:09:06.011
through a super rigorous test.

00:09:06.078 --> 00:09:08.547
And I came out on
top, and feels great.

00:09:08.614 --> 00:09:11.717
This $10,000, I'm
actually gonna give

00:09:11.783 --> 00:09:12.985
it all straight to my parents.

00:09:13.052 --> 00:09:15.220
They supported me
through college as I

00:09:15.287 --> 00:09:16.389
was learning bladesmithing.

00:09:16.455 --> 00:09:17.656
And they're both
getting ready to retire,

00:09:17.723 --> 00:09:20.960
so it's all going to them.

